From 089ad7de3dbbeae06410419023775caa4b16616e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vadzim Dziadziulia <vadzim.dziadziulia@keemail.me>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 20:42:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] [cert-manager] Update to 1.20

cert-manager 1.18 is EOL (2026-03-10) and supports Kubernetes 1.29-1.33, but OKD
4.21 is Kubernetes 1.34. 1.20 covers 1.32-1.35, clearing both 4.21 and 4.22 in
one bump. (No cert-manager-1.21 branch exists upstream.)

Four changes beyond the submodule refs were needed, each found by following
AGENTS.md rather than by inspection:

- patches/operator.patch regenerated: its hunk context pinned 1.18 via
  olm.skipRange, so git am -3 failed on the 1.20 CSV base.
- Same patch now relaxes the Makefile validate-semver guard, new in 1.20, which
  accepts only bare X.Y.Z and rejects the ${MAJOR}.${MINOR}.0-${DATE} that
  common.sh passes as BUNDLE_VERSION. A pre-release suffix is valid semver.
- Containerfiles bumped to go-toolset:1.26. cert-manager-1.20 declares go 1.26.0
  and jetstack release-1.20 declares go 1.25.0; both exceed the current 1.24, so
  build_containers could not have succeeded.
- operator.Containerfile builds the binary directly instead of via `make build`.
  From 1.20 the build target depends on generate, which runs
  hack/update-clientgen.sh and needs k8s.io/code-generator; that is not vendored,
  so under -mod=vendor the image build fails on client-gen, lister-gen,
  informer-gen and applyconfiguration-gen. The generated code is already
  committed. The replacement mirrors the ENV block and `go build` line Red Hat
  uses for this operator's operand images (rhcatalog.sh containerfiles
  cert-manager 4.21).

Verified: build_containers builds all four images; make bundle +
operator-sdk bundle validate pass; the four operand images were rebuilt for
amd64 on an OKD 4.21 cluster and pushed, and OLM on that cluster resolves the
alpha channel head to this bundle and generates an InstallPlan for it.
Not verified: the InstallPlan was deliberately left unapproved, so the operator
itself has not been run.
